        "The Bach Long Glass Bridge stands in the Moc Chau Island resort, in Ta So village, Muong Sang commune, Moc Chau. Opened on 28 April 2022, the structure totals about 632 m: a 290 m glass walkway links two mountainsides while a 342 m path runs along the cliff, and at its launch Guinness World Records recognised it as the world's longest glass pedestrian bridge. Its deck of multi-layer tempered glass hangs roughly 150 m above the valley floor, letting visitors look straight down onto the forest and ravine below. To reach the bridge, guests ride a glass lift or an escalator through a cave — an impressive experience in itself. Beyond the bridge, Moc Chau Island offers entertainment, sightseeing and dining. From the span, the view opens onto ranks of mountains, terraced fields and villages of the Moc Chau plateau. It draws thrill-seekers and young travellers and has become a new tourism emblem of Son La.",
